1
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Part Time Pal is a animation, comedy film directed by William Hanna.

2
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Tom is given the task of guarding the fridge during the night by Mammy-Two-Shoes, but as soon as he has
started he is tricked by Jerry into falling into the basement, where he lands in a barrel of cider.

3
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Now drunk, Tom staggers around in the house getting up to no good with Jerry.

4
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Mammy Two-Shoes (voice) (uncredited), played by Lillian Randolph.

5
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Tom (voice) (uncredited), played by Harry Lang.

6
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Tubby the Tuba is a 1947 American animated short film from Paramount
Pictures, directed by George Pal as part of his Puppetoons series.

7
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:50,000
It was based on the original song by Paul Tripp and George Kleinsinger.

8
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,000
The film features narration by Victor Jory.

9
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
The film received an Academy Award nomination for Best
Animated Short, but lost to Warner Bros.

10
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Cartoons' Merrie Melodies cartoon Tweetie Pie.

11
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:58,000
A feature-length version was released in 1975 by AVCO Embassy.

12
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:30,000
The 1987 compilation feature, The Puppetoon Movie,
featured the original short in its entirety.

13
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:02,000
The film explores themes of cartoon cat, cartoon mouse, intoxication.

14
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:34,000
The tone is lighthearted.
